---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const B = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Standards"
  description="The open standards of Extended Matrix: the CRMem ontology, the em.json file format and the SKOS vocabularies, with their permanent identifiers."
>
  <section class="std">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="tag">Standards</span>
      <h1>What Extended Matrix publishes for reuse.</h1>
      <p class="std__lede">
        Three pieces are meant to be reused outside our own tools: the
        ontology that says what the Extended Matrix asserts, the file format
        that carries a study, and the controlled vocabularies the method
        originates. Each has a permanent identifier under
        <code>w3id.org/extendedmatrix</code>, a human-readable page and a
        machine-readable form.
      </p>

      <div class="std__grid">
        <article class="std__card">
          <h2>CRMem — the ontology</h2>
          <p>
            The Extended Matrix extension of CIDOC CRM: the terms the method
            needs that the CIDOC CRM family does not provide, above all the
            virtual stratigraphic units and the reasoning that supports them.
            Every class sits beneath a class of the reference family.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={`${B}/ontology/`}>Classes &amp; properties declarations</a></li>
            <li><a href={`${B}/ontology/em.ttl`}>Turtle</a> · <a href={`${B}/ontology/em.rdf`}>RDF/XML</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://docs.extendedmatrix.org/projects/s3dgraphy/en/v1.6/crmem.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">What it contains and why</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="std__pid">Permanent URI: <code>https://w3id.org/extendedmatrix/ontology</code></p>
        </article>

        <article class="std__card">
          <h2>em.json — the file format</h2>
          <p>
            The container of an Extended Matrix study: the stratigraphic graph,
            its sources and paradata, its resources and the versions it is
            consistent with. The same file is read and written by s3dgraphy and
            by every tool of the ecosystem.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={`${B}/spec/em-json/`}>Specification</a></li>
            <li><a href={`${B}/schemas/`}>JSON schemas</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23642464" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Citable release on Zenodo</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="std__pid">Permanent URI: <code>https://w3id.org/extendedmatrix/spec/em-json</code></p>
        </article>

        <article class="std__card">
          <h2>Vocabularies</h2>
          <p>
            Small controlled vocabularies in SKOS that the Extended Matrix
            originates and maintains, each with a human-readable page and its
            Turtle serialisation. Licensed CC BY 4.0 unless a module states
            otherwise.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href={`${B}/vocab/`}>All modules</a></li>
          </ul>
          <p class="std__pid">Permanent URI: <code>https://w3id.org/extendedmatrix/vocab/</code></p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="std__note">
        Browsers that open a permanent URI reach the page; software that asks
        for RDF reaches the serialisation. The pages are generated from the
        sources in <a href="https://github.com/ExtendedMatrix/s3Dgraphy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">s3dgraphy</a>
        and in the vocabularies repository, so what you read is what the tools use.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .std { padding: 3rem 0 4rem; }
  .std__lede { max-width: 46em; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .std__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(270px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 2rem 0; }
  .std__card { border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.12); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem; }
  .std__card h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .std__card ul { padding-left: 1.1rem; margin: .8rem 0; }
  .std__card li { margin: .25rem 0; }
  .std__pid { font-size: .85rem; opacity: .8; word-break: break-all; }
  .std__note { max-width: 46em; font-size: .95rem; opacity: .85; }
</style>
